Package: hd-qemu-kvm
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3, python3-debconf, debconf (>= 0.5) | debconf-2.0, hd-base,
 qemu-system-x86, qemu-system-modules-spice, qemu-system-modules-opengl, qemu-utils, ovmf,
 libvirt-daemon-system, libvirt-clients, bridge-utils
Suggests: virt-manager
Conflicts: qemu-system-gui
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian Qemu/KVM support
 Installs Qemu with KVM, with the spice and OpenGL modules for the graphics of
 virtual machines, the UEFI firmware OVMF and libvirt, and sets them up to
 run virtual machines on the network through the bridge br0.
 .
 The first installation makes the wired interfaces that the administrator
 chooses ports of the bridge br0, with the network commands of hd-base.
 libvirtd only listens on its local sockets and stores secrets without
 encryption. A reboot of the host shuts the running guests down and starts
 them again, so it reboots them too. The module br_netfilter is loaded with the traffic over bridges
 kept out of the firewall, and new users connect virsh and virt-manager to
 qemu:///system. Adding users to the groups libvirt and kvm is left to the
 administrator.
